## 1). Insertion Sort Algorithm 
---Insertion Sort picks one element at a time and places it in its correct position in the already sorted part of the array.

Algorithm
-Start from the second element (i = 1).
-Store the current element in key.
-Compare key with elements before it.(WHICH IS ASSUME SORTED)
-Shift larger elements one position to the right.
-Insert key at its correct position.
-Repeat until the array is sorted.
[5, 2, 4, 6, 1, 3]

### Step 1
[5] 2 4 6 1 3

* `5` is considered sorted.
* Pick `2`.
* Compare `2` with `5`.
* Since `2 < 5`, shift `5` to the right. //[2, 5, 4, 6, 1, 3]

### Step 2
Current array:   [2, 5] 4 6 1 3

* Pick `4`.
* Compare with `5`.
* `4 < 5`, so shift `5`.  //[2, _, 5, 6, 1, 3]

* Compare `4` with `2`.
* `4 > 2`, so insert `4`. //[2, 4, 5, 6, 1, 3]

### Step 3
Current array: [2, 4, 5] 6 1 3

* Pick `6`.
* `6` is greater than `5`.
* No shifting needed.  //[2, 4, 5, 6, 1, 3]

### Step 4
Current array: [2, 4, 5, 6] 1 3

* Pick `1`.
* Compare with `6`, `5`, `4`, `2`.
* Shift all of them one position right.  [_, 2, 4, 5, 6, 3]

* Insert `1`.  [1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 3]

### Step 5
Current array: [1, 2, 4, 5, 6] 3

* Pick `3`.
* Compare with `6`, `5`, `4`.
* Shift them right.
* Insert `3` after `2`.  //[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]  ✅ Sorted Array

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int arr[] = {5,2,4,6,1,3};
        for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++){
            int key = arr[i];// current element
            int j = i-1; // previous index
            
            // shift larger element to right side
            while(j>=0 && arr[j]>key){
                arr[j+1] = arr[j];
                j--;
            }
            //place key at correct position
            arr[j+1] = key;
            
        }
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            System.out.print(arr[i]+" "); // [1,2,3,4,5,6]
        }

| Case                        | Complexity |
| --------------------------- | ---------- |
| Best Case (already sorted)  | O(n)       |
| Average Case                | O(n²)      |
| Worst Case (reverse sorted) | O(n²)      |

    }
}
